      ":question/problem": "![](images/60/605c5def8bc643f0f601f89b9f8d7b556ac94206867dbe8904ef746c83f02fc0.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the vector $a.$ Which of the following diagrams shows the vector $\\frac{3}{2}a?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that $\\frac{3}{2}a$ must be parallel to $a.$\nNow, we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $\\frac{3}{2}a$ is $\\frac{3}{2}$ of the magnitude of $a.$\n\n- Vectors $a$ and $\\frac{3}{2}a$ have the same direction since the factor $\\frac{3}{2}$ is positive.\n\nTherefore, the correct diagram is the following.\n\n![](images/59/591682cfbe0f50347d88f894f4c2b740fca140e8a93838f5c53022f9f50ee6da.png)"
